1
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:09,800
Imagine pointing your smartphone at almost anything and
instantly discovering information about it.

2
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:14,667
A product, a plant, a famous landmark, or even
a page of handwritten notes.

3
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:21,533
Google Lens makes this possible using artificial
intelligence and visual search technology.

4
00:00:21,567 --> 00:00:23,833
But how does it actually work?

5
00:00:23,867 --> 00:00:28,667
In this video, we'll explore the technology
behind Google Lens, step by step.

6
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,900
Google Lens is a visual search tool developed
by Google.

7
00:00:33,933 --> 00:00:39,900
Instead of typing words into a search bar, you can use your
camera or an existing image to search for information.

8
00:00:39,933 --> 00:00:46,467
Google Lens analyzes what it sees and helps
you discover relevant results.

9
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:57,267
It can recognize objects, identify landmarks, extract text,
translate signs, and help you find similar products online.

10
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:02,200
The idea is simple: use an image as your
search query.

11
00:01:02,233 --> 00:01:09,700
This makes searching more natural, especially when you don't know the name of
something or when describing it with words would be difficult.

12
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:17,400
When you point your camera at an object, the
first step is capturing an image.

13
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:25,167
The system processes visual information such as shapes, colors, textures,
patterns, and the relationships between different parts of the image.

14
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:31,700
Machine learning models analyze this information to
develop an understanding of what might be present.

15
00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:39,000
For example, when you scan a sneaker, the system can
identify visual features that resemble footwear.

16
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:44,400
It may also distinguish specific characteristics,
such as its color, style, and design.

17
00:01:44,433 --> 00:01:49,167
These visual clues help the system understand
what to search for next.

18
00:01:50,933 --> 00:02:01,833
One of the technologies that makes Google Lens possible is computer vision, a field
of artificial intelligence focused on understanding images and videos.

19
00:02:01,867 --> 00:02:07,467
AI models learn visual patterns from large
collections of training examples.

20
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:14,667
When a new image is analyzed, the model uses its learned patterns
to recognize possible objects and visual features.

21
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:23,167
Modern visual search systems can also use sophisticated models to
understand how different elements of an image relate to one another.

22
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:31,633
Rather than simply looking for an identical picture, the system can use visual
similarities and context to help identify relevant information.

23
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:38,933
After analyzing the image, Google Lens can use its visual
understanding to find relevant search results.

24
00:02:38,967 --> 00:02:43,467
Let's imagine that you scan a pair of
sneakers.

25
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:49,833
Google Lens may show visually similar shoes, product
listings, shopping information, and useful web pages.

26
00:02:49,867 --> 00:03:00,667
The results can help you learn more about the style or find
places where similar products are available.

27
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:05,900
Visual search is especially useful for clothing,
furniture, accessories, and everyday objects.

28
00:03:05,933 --> 00:03:17,167
Instead of trying to describe the exact shape and color of a product,
you can simply show the camera what you're looking for.

29
00:03:17,967 --> 00:03:21,600
Google Lens can also work with text inside
images.

30
00:03:21,633 --> 00:03:29,033
This is made possible by optical character recognition, commonly known as
OCR, combined with other language-processing technologies.

31
00:03:29,067 --> 00:03:43,433
When you point your camera at a printed page or sign, Lens can detect the
text and allow you to copy it, search for it, or translate it.

32
00:03:43,467 --> 00:03:52,000
Imagine traveling to another country and seeing a sign
written in a language you don't understand.

33
00:03:52,033 --> 00:03:58,367
Google Lens can help translate that text and
display the result on your screen.

34
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:05,633
You can also use it to copy information from books, notes,
and documents without typing everything manually.

35
00:04:06,667 --> 00:04:09,700
Google Lens can be useful in many everyday
situations.

36
00:04:09,733 --> 00:04:17,667
If you see an unfamiliar plant, you can scan it to
explore possible matches and learn more about it.

37
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:25,700
If you're visiting a famous location, visual search may help
you identify a landmark and discover its history.

38
00:04:25,733 --> 00:04:31,867
If you see a product you like, you can search for
similar items without knowing the brand or model.

39
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:39,033
You can also translate menus, copy printed text, and search
for information related to objects around you.

40
00:04:39,067 --> 00:04:43,633
However, AI recognition isn't always perfect.

41
00:04:43,667 --> 00:04:49,933
Results can vary depending on image quality,
lighting, and the information available.

42
00:04:51,233 --> 00:04:53,433
Using Google Lens is straightforward.

43
00:04:53,467 --> 00:05:01,933
Open the Google app or another supported place where Lens
is available, and select the Google Lens icon.

44
00:05:01,967 --> 00:05:08,167
You can point your camera at something you want to explore
or choose an existing picture from your device.

45
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:13,067
Position the object clearly inside the camera view
and capture or select the image as needed.

46
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:17,067
Lens will analyze it and display relevant
options or search results.

47
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:28,967
Depending on the content, you can explore matching products, copy
text, translate words, or discover additional information.

48
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:38,500
Google Lens brings together computer vision, artificial intelligence, text
recognition, and visual search to make everyday information easier to discover.

49
00:05:38,533 --> 00:05:42,767
Instead of searching only with words, we can
now explore the world using images.

50
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:50,433
From identifying objects to translating text, visual search
is changing how we interact with information.

51
00:05:50,467 --> 00:05:56,633
Google Lens is one example of how AI connects
the physical world with digital knowledge.

52
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:06,667
If you liked this video, please like, share
and subscribe to the channel. Thank you!
